# Everything here is sent to the Docker daemon before the first instruction
# runs, so anything large and unused is pure latency on every single build.
#
# The big one is share/ollama/models: it is the default bind-mount target for
# OLLAMA_MODELS_HOST_DIR, so any machine that has run this stack has tens of
# gigabytes of model blobs sitting there. A local `docker build` was uploading
# a 33.88 GB context to produce an image that never touches it — the models
# arrive at runtime through the volume, never through a COPY. (CI never
# noticed: the directory is gitignored, so a fresh checkout has none of it.)
share/

**/node_modules
.git
.github

# Produced by the frontend-builder stage inside the image. A stale local copy
# is never wanted and can only mask a broken build.
frontend/dist/

# Tooling, editor and agent scratch directories.
.playwright-mcp/
.claude/
.superpowers/
.ua/

# Not referenced by any build stage (TUNING.md is COPY'd, so it stays).
ky50p.png
fonts/
docs/
